"## Summary\n\nWire-nodes follow-up 35: devstack 32's request about `If-Match: \"0\"`, under the orchestrator's revised provisional ruling.\n- **Sessions:**\n  - **The first** launched at 19:16 EST on 2026-11-03, and stopped at 19:39 at the brief's precondition.\n  - **The resume** (`### Resume 1`) ran from 19:40 to 20:01.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 3 commits and 4 owned files, +388/−8. The production change is three lines in `internal/nodes/nodes.go`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree, current `main` (`d937bd65`) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/nodes.mk nodes-lint nodes-test nodes-integration nodes-build`;\n    - `go test -count=1 -tags integration ./internal/nodes/... ./internal/httpapi/... ./internal/exits/...`, and the zero-version tests by name;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/e2e/...` and `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...`, for the consumers;\n    - `make go-lint`, `go vet ./...`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** no Docker, no reservation, and no schema, contract or contract-version change.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The first session's stop was correct.** The brief made \"no resource can have version 0\" a precondition.\n  - **The lane's finding:** explicit inserts may store `resource_version` 0 in `nodes` and `exits`, while production enrollment defaults to 1, and `db.UpdateWithVersion` matches `\"0\"` against a zero row.\n  - Its dated note keeps the isolated-database counterexample, byte for byte.\n  - spec §14.5 and the contract give zero no special meaning, and set no minimum version;\n  - so `\"0\"` is compared like any other version;\n  - no schema change and no positive-version invariant.\n- **The change:** `ParseIfMatch` no longer rejects zero before the lookup. Its decimal parser, error branches and every caller's comparison are unchanged.\n  - **A row at version 0** matches `\"0\"` and is written. Its version advances as usual.\n  - **Every other row** gets the ordinary 412 `RESOURCE_VERSION_CONFLICT`, with `details.current_resource_version`.\n  - **Unchanged:** a missing or empty header still gets 428. A malformed value still gets today's 412, now also tested for leading zeros, weak and list tags, a missing quote and overflow.\n- **Tests:**\n  - **Four guarded routes:** capacity PATCH, revoke POST, retire DELETE and publication PUT.\n    - Zero and stale non-zero conflicts return the current version, and change nothing: no node, exit, certificate or enrollment state, operation, audit, outbox or idempotency record.\n    - The same key and body with the read `ETag` then succeed once.\n  - **A zero-row test:** a row inserted at version 0 reads back as `ETag \"0\"`, accepts it, and advances to 1. A replay writes nothing more.\n  - **Standalone service entry points** cover all six audited `ParseIfMatch` call sites, including `exits.SetPublication`'s validation-only parse.\n- **Hand-off,** nonblocking: devstack's comment above `publisherTrace32` (`tests/e2e/publisher_proof_test.go`) still describes the old rejection. Its two-shape check stays compatible. Routed to devstack's next follow-up.\n\n"
